    (:adr
      :id "D44"
      :shortcode "D44"
      :title "Canonical Machine-Native ASN Decisions and Dual-Projection Governance"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Markdown ADRs impose a 75 percent token tax on agent context and prevent deterministic AST querying in memory engines."
      :drivers [
        "Context preservation and token economy (d-1eed)"
        "Deterministic AST queryability in memory engine (mem/engine.asl)"
        "Strict delimiter balance validation (asl check)"
        "M2M pure machine protocol vs on-demand human projection"
      ]
      :decision "Establish canonical .asn storage for all ADRs in .asl/mem/decisions/ and provide an on-demand Markdown projector in mem/src/projector.asl."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "d-1eed" "d34"]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Reduces decision context loading overhead by 75 to 80 percent")
        (:pos "Enables instant typed S-expression queries across decisions in mem/engine.asl")
        (:pos "Full compiler validation of all decisions via asl check")
        (:pos "Preserves human inspectability via on-demand Markdown projection")
        (:neg "Requires on-demand projection step when generating human documentation showcases")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D45"
      :shortcode "D45"
      :title "Sovereign Task Pool, Session Leases, Crash Recovery and Machine Notes Ledger"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/memory"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Ad-hoc task discoveries during execution sessions are frequently lost upon session completion or disconnection. Uncoordinated multi-agent sessions risk mutating overlapping files without deterministic lease exclusivity. Architectural observations decay in chat logs rather than persisting in machine-queryable memory. Furthermore, hyphenated zero-padded shortcodes impose an unnecessary 50 percent token penalty on BPE tokenizers."
      :drivers [
        "Durable Shared Task Pool: zero lost tasks or abandoned work items across agent sessions (d40)"
        "Exclusive Session Leases: blast-radius file locking prevents concurrent mutation collisions"
        "Deterministic Crash Recovery: resumption from exact step-index and handoff-context checkpoints"
        "Machine-Native Notes Ledger (.asl/mem/notes.asn): typed persistent observations with dual-projection"
        "2-Token Compact Shortcode Basis: prefix plus number (d1..d44, c1..c4, n1..n10) cuts token tax by 50 percent (c4)"
      ]
      :decision "Establish durable shared task pool with time-bounded session leases and CAS crash recovery in mem/src/tasks.asl; implement machine-native notes ledger (.asl/mem/notes.asn) and engine (mem/src/notes.asl) with on-demand Markdown projection; and support 2-token compact alias resolution across all memory registries."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "d40" "d44"]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Guarantees zero lost tasks and seamless recovery across aborted or killed sessions")
        (:pos "Eliminates concurrent file mutation race conditions via blast-radius session locks")
        (:pos "Establishes persistent on-disk machine memory for technical observations and discoveries")
        (:pos "Reduces shortcode token consumption by 50 percent across all LLM prompts and S-expressions")
        (:neg "Requires active renewal of session leases for long-running batch operations")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D46"
      :shortcode "D46"
      :title "Three-Tier Task Lifecycle Architecture, Bare-Symbol 2-Token Basis, and Deprecation of Sigil Prefixes"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/task-and-governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Ad-hoc subtasks, active phase milestones, and long-term backlog candidates lack clean lifecycle isolation, polluting agent prompts with irrelevant context. Furthermore, using leading colons (:c1, :d45) for shortcodes causes syntax and conceptual collisions with ASN map property keys (:id, :why), while sigil prefixes (@d45, #d45) incur a 50 percent tokenization penalty in modern BPE tokenizers."
      :drivers [
        "Three-Tier Lifecycle Separation: Backlog (backlog.asn) vs Active Wave Roadmap (phase_*.asn) vs In-Flight Agent Memory (InFlight.asn)"
        "Zero-Token Backlog Overhead: parked tasks consume 0 tokens during active execution waves"
        "Pure Bare-Symbol 2-Token Basis: shortcodes are atomic bare symbols (c1..c4, d1..d46, n1..n10, t388-1) without colons or quotes"
        "Property vs Symbol Disambiguation: property keys begin with colon (:prop), reference symbols do not ([c1 c2 d46])"
        "Sigil Deprecation: @ and # are permanently purged from all references, package names, and identifiers"
      ]
      :decision "Formalize the three-tier task storage and lifecycle model; establish bare atomic symbols as the universal 2-token shortcode standard across all registries, S-expressions, and agent communications; and permanently deprecate @ and # sigils for referencing invariants, decisions, notes, and tasks."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "d40" "d45"]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates prompt bloat by isolating dormant backlog items in .asl/mem/tasks/backlog.asn")
        (:pos "Strictly achieves 2 tokens per identifier across cl100k and o200k tokenizers")
        (:pos "Eliminates grammar ambiguity between property keys and atomic value references in S-expressions")
        (:pos "Preserves 100 percent backward compatibility via transparent alias normalization in asl-engine")
        (:neg "Requires explicit migration of legacy @d-XXXX mentions in documentation and skills")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D47"
      :shortcode "D47"
      :title "Codebase Lexical Token Profiler, Hotspot Forensic Audit, and Rational Boundary Compaction Paradigm"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "As codebases evolve, identifiers and keywords accumulate verbose multi-token English compounds (string-contains? [4 tok], string-starts-with? [5 tok], string-from-int64 [5 tok], :rationale [3 tok]), violating the 1-to-2 token basis (c4, d46). Furthermore, AI agents lack resident tooling to profile token distribution, identify token monsters, locate file hotspots, and apply deterministic compaction rules across arbitrary projects."
      :drivers [
        "Full-Spectrum Token Auditing: resident tool capable of scanning all ASL and ASN files in single sub-second pass"
        "Multi-Dimensional Decomposition: global metrics, file hotspots, token monsters, and recurring collocations"
        "Rational Boundary & Local Autonomy (d34): distinguishing wire boundary protocols from local domain internals"
        "Concrete Compaction Modalities & 1-to-2 Token Aliases (txt/*, v/*, opt/*, str/*)"
        "Cross-Project Portability: self-contained executable rules applicable to any ASL/ASN repository"
      ]
      :decision "Implement full-codebase multi-dimensional token profiling in asl-engine (:tokens :mode \"all\") and CLI (asl tokens --all, asl tokens --paradigm); formalize the Rational Boundary Compaction Paradigm; calibrate and audit across all 995 files in the monorepo; and verify under monorepo gate."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "d34" "d46"]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Enables instant full-repository token profiling across 995 files in under 2 seconds")
        (:pos "Identifies exact file hotspots, token monsters (>= 3 tokens), and recurring 2-gram collocations")
        (:pos "Calculates potential token savings (21,902 tokens across monorepo) and suggests modular 1-to-2 token aliases")
        (:pos "Embeds the Rational Boundary Compaction Paradigm directly into CLI for standalone adoption in external projects")
        (:neg "Requires periodic codebase auditing during release cycles to maintain low token debt")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D48"
      :shortcode "D48"
      :title "Universal Sigil Eradication, Native Bare Symbol Architecture, and Zero-Sigil Invariant"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "The @ sigil was historically retained for scoped package identifiers (@genseam/...) and reference annotations (@ref:, @adr:), causing token fragmentation in BPE tokenizers and conceptual ambiguity with language primitives. Autonomous coding agents require a 100% clean, sigil-free cognitive domain where package identities and symbols are bare atomic symbols."
      :drivers [
        "Zero-Sigil Invariant (c5): complete eradication of @ and # sigils from package names, task labels, and identifiers"
        "Native Bare Symbol Packages: converting all @genseam/asl-* packages to native bare symbols (asl-codec, asl-parser, asl-mem)"
        "Keyword-Based Frame Serialization: replacing @wal:{, @v:{, @n:{, @e:{, @snap:{ with native frames wal:{, v:{, n:{, e:{, snap:{"
        "Agent Identity Normalization: replacing @scout, @coder, @reviewer with native keywords (:scout, :coder, :reviewer)"
        "BPE Token Compression: eliminating the multi-token fragmentation penalty of sigil prefixes across all models"
      ]
      :decision "Permanently eradicate the @ sigil across all package manifests, grammar registries, memory serialization engines, agent identity references, and task ledgers; enforce native bare symbols for all 35 package manifests; update manifest gate to strictly reject @ sigil package names; and establish the Zero-Sigil Invariant (c5)."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d47"]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Guarantees 100% pure native bare symbol packaging across all 35 monorepo packages")
        (:pos "Eliminates sigil splitting penalty across BPE tokenizers, saving tokens on every package and symbol reference")
        (:pos "Harmonizes memory WAL and snapshot frame formats with pure S-expression conventions")
        (:pos "Gate 1 and manifest-gate reject any reintroduction of @ sigils automatically")
        (:neg "Requires updating legacy documentation and external references that previously cited scoped names")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D49"
      :shortcode "D49"
      :title "Ambient Voice and Prompt Transliterator, Context-Primed Homophone Disambiguation, and Canonical ASN Intent Generation"
