        (:pos "Delivers sub-0.5ms resident BM25 search across monorepo AST without disk grep overhead")
        (:pos "Enables isolated in-memory VFS sandboxing for parallel agents preventing dirty state leakage")
        (:neg "Requires resident memory to hold inverted term index and token vectors")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D51"
      :shortcode "D51"
      :title "Token Efficiency Format, CamelCase Conventions, and Rationality-Flagged Grammar Registries"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Pretrained LLM tokenizers (BPE / SentencePiece) incur a heavy token-splitting penalty on hyphenated S-expression identifiers (kebab-case), splitting multi-word symbols at every hyphen. Conversely, agents operating in Lisp-like homoiconic environments default to kebab-case unless explicitly guided, wasting 20-50% tokens on composite constructs. Additionally, legacy dash-zero markers (D0001..D0050) consume 3-4 BPE tokens instead of 1, and grammar registries lacked fine-grained rationality classification."
      :drivers [
        "BPE Token Compression: CamelCase merges subwords with capital transitions, saving 20-50% tokens on composite names"
        "Capital Alphanumeric Markers: D1..D51, C1..C5, L1..L10, R1..R10 compress marker references from 4 tokens to 1 token"
        "Hybrid Naming Architecture: Reserve CamelCase for composite constructs, types, and test suites while preserving 1-to-2 token modular primitives (txt/*, v/*)"
        "Dual-Tier Rationality Annotations: Classify symbols > 2 tokens as :rationality :absolute or :contextSpecific with :contextDependent boolean"
        "Internal and Cross-Package Duplicate Prevention: Zero duplicate declarations within packages and harmonized rationales across monorepo"
        "Standard Progressive Disclosure: Integrate guidance into AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md, and on-demand agent skills"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt the Token Efficiency Format monorepo-wide: migrate marker format from dash-zero to capital alphanumeric shortcodes (D1..D51, C1..C5); establish CamelCase naming conventions for composite constructs, structs, typestates, and test suites; enforce dual-tier rationality flags in grammar registries; provide automated audit tooling (asl audit tokens, asl tokens --camel); and integrate binding guidelines across all standard agent documentation methods."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d47" "d48" "d50"]
      :tasks [
        "Task40001"
        "Task40002"
        "Task40003"
        "Task40004"
        "Task40005"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Saves 1,610 tokens across grammar registries and 25-50% on compound names throughout the codebase")
        (:pos "Reduces marker token footprint by 75% per reference across intent, roadmap, and tasks")
        (:pos "Provides deterministic guidance so autonomous agents generate token-efficient code without hesitation")
        (:pos "Preserves pure ASL zero-comment and zero-emoji invariants (C1, C2) and bare-symbol basis (C5)")
        (:neg "Requires agents to distinguish between 1-2 token atomic primitives and composite CamelCase constructs")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D52"
      :shortcode "D52"
      :title "Enriched Task Context Standard, Bidirectional ADR-Task-Intent Linkage, and Holistic Consistency Audit Engine"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "architecture/governance"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "In multi-agent autonomous engineering across backlogs, active phase plans, and in-flight session buffers, decomposing goals into atomic tasks frequently causes critical architectural context to evaporate. Motivation, usage context, expected outcomes, alternative design variations, and failure scenarios are omitted or decoupled from ADRs. Consequently, ADRs become static records lacking traceable implementation tasks, while tasks execute without explicit grounding in governing decisions. Additionally, records drift without periodic consistency verification."
      :drivers [
        "Context Preservation Invariant: Zero context loss when planning, breaking down, or triaging tasks across all 3 storage tiers"
        "Enriched Task Metadata: Standardizing motivation, purpose, usage context, expected outcomes, invariants, variations, and failure scenarios"
        "Bidirectional Traceability: Tasks declare governing ADRs (:adr, :decision); ADRs declare implementing tasks (:tasks); Intent ledger binds both"
        "Multi-Tier Consistency: Continuous alignment between Tier 1 backlog, Tier 2 phase DAG, Tier 3 in-flight session buffer, and intent"
        "Periodic Consistency Audit Engine: Self-hosted 'asl audit consistency' command verifying zero orphan records, broken links, or context voids"
        "Standard Progressive Disclosure: Codifying task templates in planning skills (asl-plan, steps-plan, asl-toolbelt) and AGENTS.md"
      ]
      :decision "Standardize the Enriched Task Context format across all monorepo task collections, backlogs, and in-flight buffers; enforce bidirectional linkage between ADRs, tasks, and intent; require all newly generated plans to capture motivation, purpose, context, outcomes, invariants, variations, and failure scenarios; and deploy the Holistic Consistency Audit Engine (asl audit consistency) to verify record synchronization deterministically."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51"]
      :tasks [
        "Task40101"
        "Task40102"
        "Task40103"
        "Task40104"
        "Task40105"
        "Task40106"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Ensures all autonomous agents operate with complete epistemic context during implementation and recovery")
        (:pos "Unifies backlog, active phase, and in-flight schemas under a single coherent specification")
        (:pos "Catches broken ADR references, orphan tasks, and missing metadata via automated consistency audit")
        (:neg "Requires planners to provide richer metadata upfront when formulating work items")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D53"
      :shortcode "D53"
      :title "Agent Responsibility Paradigm, Operational Epistemic Primitives, Adaptive Action DAG, and Pure ASL Toolchain Migration"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-09"
      :cluster "agent-epistemology/runtime"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Autonomous agents governed exclusively by negative bounding constraints lack intrinsic motivation, frequently succumbing to minimal/vacuous execution, premature task settlement, or surrogate optimization (loosening test assertions, inserting stubs, swallowing exceptions). Crucial epistemic disciplines—anti-hallucination grounding, context budget management, adversarial reflection, and reality reconciliation—are relegated to informal prompt advice rather than enforced as discrete, typed operational steps in an execution DAG. When unexpected errors occur, rigid linear plans fail without dynamic recovery. Additionally, maintaining a 6,166-line legacy Bash host runner (./asl/asl) directly breaches the Zero-Foreign File Policy (Gate 4) and causes severe cognitive context divergence across multi-agent swarms."
      :drivers [
        "Responsibility as the Core Paradigm Unit: Replacing anthropomorphic roleplay with a teleological responsibility vector (User-Centric Intent Fidelity) where true user problem resolution takes absolute precedence over mechanical green checks."
        "Discrete Epistemic Steps: Codifying GroundFact, ContextBudget, AdversarialReflect, and ReconcileReality as first-class typed operational steps within the agent Action DAG."
        "Adaptive Action DAG & Closed Refixing Loop: Enabling agents to halt upon intermediate gate failures, execute RAM VFS rollback (:discard), diagnose root causes, and dynamically recalculate recovery DAGs under a bounded retry budget (<= 3)."
        "Model-Native Paradigm Language: Defining an immutable Core Kernel of axioms (C1-C5, D34, D51) paired with modular, composable paradigm slices (:slice :scout, :slice :implementer, :slice :auditor, :slice :transliterator)."
        "Pure ASL Toolchain & 100% Bash Eradication: Porting all verification gates, runners, and CLI routers from ./asl/asl into pure AgentScript modules (packages/asl-gates, packages/asl-cli, packages/asl-sh), reducing the launcher to a 5-line POSIX shim."
        "Co-located ASN Skills & Third-Party Projection: Storing skills as canonical native ASN specifications co-located with packages, projected build-time into Markdown SKILL.md micro-protocols for external agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Factory Droid, Windsurf, OpenHands) with deterministic 1-line ASN receipts, explicit external refixing directives, and automated export drift reconciliation."
        "Dual-Tier Task Ledger & Observability: Bounding git-tracked global intent/backlogs and ephemeral local agent session folders (.asl/mem/sessions/<session-id>/) with queue positioning, lifecycle timestamps (:created-at, :queuedAt), and automated session action cleanup."
      ]
      :decision "Adopt Responsibility and User-Centric Intent Fidelity as the foundational paradigm unit in harness/paradigm.asn; elevate anti-hallucination grounding, context budget throttling, adversarial reflection, and reality reconciliation into discrete, executable steps in the Action DAG; implement dynamic adaptive replanning and closed refixing with RAM VFS rollback triggered by gate failures; standardize the Core Kernel plus Modular Slices paradigm language; execute the comprehensive migration of the 6,166-line Bash toolbelt into pure AgentScript modules across asl-gates, asl-cli, and asl-sh; project canonical ASN skills into Markdown micro-protocols with deterministic receipts and refixing protocols for third-party agents; and establish the Dual-Tier Task Ledger with session isolation, queue timestamps, and automated ephemeral cleanup."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51" "d52"]
      :tasks [
        "Task40201"
        "Task40202"
        "Task40203"
        "Task40204"
        "Task40205"
        "Task40206"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Transforms agent execution from fragile linear scripts into resilient, self-correcting epistemic workflows")
        (:pos "Eliminates multi-language cognitive load by making all tools, gates, and compiler pipelines pure ASL")
        (:pos "Ensures all skills remain synchronized with canonical ASN specifications without manual markdown upkeep")
        (:pos "Enables safe multi-agent concurrency with clean git history and automated session cleanup")
        (:neg "Requires agents to allocate dedicated DAG steps for pre-mutation grounding and adversarial reflection")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D54"
      :shortcode "D54"
      :title "Systemic Gap Remediation, Ground Truth Hardening, E2E Reconciliation, and Pure ASL Toolchain Migration"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/reconciliation"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "A comprehensive multi-agent audit revealed 64 systemic incongruities across the monorepo: (1) Vacuous verification vectors where gates passed on hardcoded boolean true, empty test suites passed without assertions, and Gate 5 skipped the 19 integration test suites in tests/ allowing 8 E2E scripts to silently rot; (2) Governance drift where Phase 402 tasks were prematurely declared complete despite 6,381 lines of legacy Bash remaining in asl/asl; (3) Memory and task schema fragmentation where TaskRecord lacked D52 enriched fields, effort/risk dimensions, and runtime collision checks; and (4) Broken runtime eviction in the daemon due to a seconds-versus-milliseconds TTL calculation error."
      :drivers [
        "Empirical Ground Truth & Vacuity Eradication: Strict enforcement that all gates execute physical operating system commands with verifiable non-zero assertion counts and genuine process exit codes."
        "E2E Integration Test Reconciliation: Reconnecting the 19 test scripts in tests/ to Gate 5, eliminating obsolete .md references, and resolving shortcode mismatches."
        "Enriched Task Context Standard (D52): Extending the in-memory TaskRecord struct with :motivation, :purpose, :context, :outcomes, :invariants, :adr, :decision, :effort, and :risk."
        "Cybernetic Anti-Collision & Stigmergic Coordination: Enforcing file boundary locks (:owns) and dynamic collision detection (task-owns-intersect?) to prevent parallel agent write races."
        "Homeostatic Closed Refixing State Machine: Implementing bounded error self-healing (ReconcileFail -> VFS Discard -> Error Extraction -> Targeted Refix <= 3) without gate weakening."
        "Pure AgentScript Self-Hosting: Incrementally porting all remaining audit, gate, and CLI routing logic from monolithic Bash into native compiled ASL packages."
      ]
      :decision "Establish Wave 55 and Phase 403 as the definitive remediation program for all 64 systemic gaps: eliminate hardcoded true literals in agent and worker loops; reject zero-assertion test suites; repair the 21-day TTL calculation in asl-engine; connect canonical svg-transpile to vdom; reconcile and restore all 8 failing E2E test scripts; bind E2E execution to Gate 5 and byte-level skill parity to Gate 7; expand TaskRecord in mem/tasks.asl with full D52 attributes and effort/risk dimensions; operationalize anti-collision task leasing; integrate anti_hallucination and pre-mortem into the coding pipeline; implement the closed refixing loop with VFS discard; update third-party skill distribution; and complete the incremental migration of asl/asl to pure AgentScript."
      :invariants ["c1" "c2" "c3" "c4" "c5" "d34" "d46" "d51" "d52"]
      :tasks [
        "Task40301"
        "Task40302"
        "Task40303"
        "Task40304"
        "Task40305"
        "Task40306"
        "Task40307"
        "Task40308"
        "Task40309"
        "Task40310"
        "Task40311"
        "Task40312"
        "Task40313"
        "Task40314"
        "Task40315"
        "Task40316"
        "Task40317"
        "Task40318"
        "Task40319"
        "Task40320"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Completely closes the gap between declarative governance and physical disk reality")
        (:pos "Eliminates the risk of silent regressions by binding all integration tests to CI gates")
        (:pos "Ensures all autonomous agents operate with full context, preventing context evaporation")
        (:pos "Provides robust multi-agent concurrency without buffer overwrites or write races")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining and executing both unit and full E2E test suites during verification")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D55"
      :shortcode "D55"
      :title "Multi-Dialect Shell Transpilation, Dialect-Aware Process Execution and Toolplane Integration"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "execution/toolplane"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Autonomous agents execute tasks across diverse host operating environments and heterogeneous CLI tools requiring specific shell dialects (POSIX sh, Bash, Zsh, Dash, PowerShell). In a pure AgentScript monorepo enforcing zero foreign files (Gate 4), executing raw bash scripts without formal AST abstraction causes unpredictable failures on POSIX-restricted platforms (such as macOS /bin/sh), breaks array or pipefail semantics, and creates non-reproducible subshell execution. Furthermore, existing shell transpilation is limited to linear pipes, lacking compound conditionals, dialect switches, and structured AST pipelines."
      :drivers [
        "Dialect Parity Invariant: Deterministic execution across POSIX, Bash, and Zsh without foreign syntax leakage"
        "Structured Shell AST: Transpilation between pure ASN S-expressions and dialect-specific shell scripts"
        "Dialect-Aware Process Execution: Supervised process plane support for :dialect flag with isolated environments"
        "Toolplane Integration: Native CLI commands (asl transpile-sh) and batch RPC operations (:shTranspile)"
        "Token Efficiency Standard (D51): Zero kebab-case identifiers, 100% CamelCase types and alphanumeric markers (T411-1..T411-6, D55)"
      ]
      :decision "Extend the AgentScript codec and execution engine with native multi-dialect shell transpilation and dialect-aware process routing. Codify ShellDialect and DialectFeatures typestates in grammar registries; implement bidirectional transpilation (asn-to-sh-dialect and sh-to-asn-dialect); add :dialect support to :procSpawn and :exec; and expose the native asl transpile-sh command."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52"]
      :tasks [
        "T4111"
        "T4112"
        "T4113"
        "T4114"
        "T4115"
        "T4116"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates shell dialect mismatch errors in macOS and Linux container environments")
        (:pos "Allows agents to generate high-density ASN shell expressions that compile deterministically to target shells")
        (:pos "Guarantees full alignment with D51 CamelCase and D52 enriched task context standards")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining dialect syntax matrices across POSIX, Bash, and Zsh grammar rules")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D56"
      :shortcode "D56"
      :title "Holistic Tool & Paradigm Audit, CamelCase Token Optimization, and In-Memory Compensating Sagas"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/optimization"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Autonomous agents face friction across four compounding dimensions: token bloat from legacy kebab-case, in-memory irreversible mutations lacking rollback, epistemic drift in context windows, and sub-optimal division of labor."
      :drivers [
        "Token Economy Arbitrage (D51): Universal adoption of camelCase and PascalCase for all internal IDs, structs, and test suites, saving 25% to 50% BPE tokens"
        "Zero-Mutation VFS Invariant: Pure functional branch overlays with two-phase CAS commits and O(1) abort-branch discarding"
        "Compensating Sagas for In-Memory Coupling: Every side-effect-bearing memory operation must register an explicit reverse destructor"
        "Epistemic Time-Travel (D12): Clean context slicing and checkpointed session rollback via asl task recover"
        "Architectural Layer Stratification (L0-L3): Strict separation of core primitives, substrates, runtime, and cognitive harness"
      ]
      :decision "Codify Phase412 as the canonical holistic audit and optimization baseline. Mandate camelCase for all internal identifiers, task labels, and non-exposed constructs monorepo-wide. Implement Compensating Sagas (TwoPhaseAction with cleanupHandler) across the in-memory engine and process plane. Formalize Epistemic Time-Travel protocols for cognitive state rollback, and enforce strict L0-L3 stratification in grammar registries."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56"]
      :tasks [
        "T412Audit"
        "T412Codec"
        "T412Sagas"
        "T412Health"
        "T412Triggers"
        "T412Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Substantial context window savings across all LLM inference operations")
        (:pos "Zero orphan processes and zero persistent memory corruption on aborted transactions")
        (:pos "Elimination of cognitive drift and amnesia loops in autonomous worker sessions")
        (:neg "Requires systematic renaming of internal symbols and strict registration of saga compensators")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D57"
      :shortcode "D57"
      :title "Semantic Subword Architecture and Morpheme-Aligned Identifiers"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/token-efficiency"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Numeric dash suffixes in task identifiers (such as T412-1) impose a BPE punctuation penalty, forcing tokenizers to allocate dedicated tokens for hyphens while providing zero functional semantic information in dependency DAGs."
      :drivers [
        "BPE Punctuation Elimination: Replace punctuation delimiters with capital subword transitions"
        "Semantic Grounding in Dependency Arrays: Encode domain purpose directly into task IDs"
        "Zero Path Collisions: Alphanumeric subwords avoid directory nesting in git refs and filesystem paths"
        "Canonical 30-Morpheme Standard: Standardize a controlled vocabulary of single-token morphemes"
