    (:adr
      :id "D58"
      :shortcode "D58"
      :title "Attention-Based Model Reliability, Deliberation Augmentation, and Intent-Driven Planning"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/reliability"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Raw attention-based models operate autoregressively in feed-forward System 1 mode without test-time deliberation. As context expands, attention weights diffuse, causing peripheral boundary neglect, uncompensated mutation leaks, schema drift, and compounding hallucinations on underspecified natural language prompts. Monolithic generation without intermediate topological planning leads to fragile implementations that fail verification gates."
      :drivers [
        "Closed Epistemic Feedback Loop: Externalize deliberation through the 4-stage loop (Awareness, Planning, Reflection, Reconciliation)"
        "Intent-Driven Planning: Expand abstract intent into invariant-bounded action DAGs with executable falsifiable gates prior to code modification"
        "Instruction Compactness & Token Density: Replace verbose natural language and JSON with compact S-expressions (ASN) delivering >70% token savings and zero-JSON syntax errors"
        "Boundary Universalism (D34, C3): Centralize wire protocols, serialization, and string escaping while preserving local domain autonomy"
        "Physical Ground-Truth Receipts: Enforce exit code 0 and non-vacuous assertions (D52) rather than speculative agent self-approvals"
      ]
      :decision "Codify Phase414 as the normative standard for attention model reliability and intent-driven planning. Mandate that all abstract agent prompts undergo formal teleological decomposition into enriched action DAGs (D52) with semantic subwords (D57). Route all tool interactions through pure ASN S-expressions and enforce boundary universalism across execution planes."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58"]
      :tasks [
        "T414Audit"
        "T414Models"
        "T414Intent"
        "T414Protocol"
        "T414Boundaries"
        "T414Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Dramatically improves reliability and determinism of LLM and SLM agent execution")
        (:pos "Sharpens attention focus by eliminating low-entropy boilerplate and punctuation tokens")
        (:pos "Prevents irreversible state corruption via mandatory compensating sagas and CAS branches")
        (:neg "Requires all agent interactions to conform to structured ASN intent schemas rather than freeform dialogue")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D59"
      :shortcode "D59"
      :title "Monorepo Memory Hierarchy, Typestate Module Decomposition, and File Organization Standard"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/organization"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "As the monorepo scaled to 35 packages and 793 source files, epistemic memory (.asl/mem/) and core source modules developed cognitive sprawl. Flat task directories mix settled historical phases with active roadmaps, while monolithic source files exceed 500-770 lines, mixing multiple distinct typestates and increasing LLM context consumption. Arbitrary file chopping is an anti-pattern that multiplies header overhead; instead, a formal typestate decomposition and tiered memory hierarchy are required."
      :drivers [
        "Typestate Cohesion Principle: Bound modules to 120-280 lines containing a single lifecycle or state machine"
        "4-Tier Epistemic Memory Hierarchy: Clear separation of Archive (Tier 0), Backlog (Tier 1), Active Waves (Tier 2), and In-Flight Sessions (Tier 3)"
        "Single Source of Truth for Decisions: Individual ADR files serve as primary truth, with decisions.asn as lightweight projection"
        "L0-L3 Package Layer Stratification: Strict downward import topology preventing circular package coupling"
        "Normalized PascalCase Subword Naming: Phase<Number><Topic>.asn and T<Number><Morpheme> task identifiers (D57)"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt the Monorepo Memory Hierarchy and Typestate Module Decomposition standard monorepo-wide as ADR-0059 (D59). Author Phase 415 to execute the typestate partitioning of 500+ line hotspots (mem/src/tasks.asl, mem/src/daemon.asl, intel/src/health.asl) into cohesive 150-250 line modules. Organize .asl/mem/ into structured tiers and enforce L0-L3 layer boundaries across all 35 packages."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59"]
      :tasks [
        "T415Audit"
        "T415TasksSplit"
        "T415DaemonSplit"
        "T415CamelTests"
        "T415AsnToolcall"
        "T415Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates attention dispersion when agents read source modules by isolating distinct lifecycles")
        (:pos "Reduces task memory context by isolating historical archive files from active working waves")
        (:pos "Prevents circular package dependencies via strict L0-L3 downward import verification")
        (:neg "Requires updating module exports and imports across affected sub-packages during decomposition")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D60"
      :shortcode "D60"
      :title "Comprehensive System for Epistemic Meta-Research, Multidimensional Design Systems, and Self-Correcting Algorithmic Optimization"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/ecosystem"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Autonomous development ecosystems require an integrated, self-correcting methodology spanning meta-research, UI/UX design systems, algorithmic optimization, and conceptual management. Unstructured research produces ungrounded assumptions, design lacks mathematical rigor across web and vector graphics (SVG), algorithm search oscillates between premature extremes and unoptimized bottlenecks, and multi-agent coordination suffers from verbose natural language instructions and unclosed feedback loops."
      :drivers [
        "Epistemic Meta-Research: Recursive hypothesis validation, cross-source triangulation, and mandatory two-pass re-investigation before implementation"
        "Mathematical Design System: Unify web and vector graphics (ASN SVG) under modular spatial grids, OkLCH color spaces, fluid typography, and line dynamics"
        "Pareto Algorithmic Optimization: Systematic search for optimal algorithms with unconstrained ceilings (E-graphs, equality saturation, AST rewriting)"
        "Compact S-Expression Intent: Formulate high-SNR conceptual models, value propositions, and toolbelt integration for external agent environments"
        "5-Stage Closed-Loop Cybernetic Lifecycle: Research Plan -> Primary Research -> Secondary Re-Investigation -> Paradigm Implementation -> Reconciliation & Continuous Audit"
      ]
      :decision "Codify ADR-0060 (D60) as the sovereign standard for the end-to-end self-correcting research, design, and algorithmic optimization ecosystem. Author Phase 416 to operationalize meta-research validation, design system tokenization, algorithmic solution search, and closed-loop reconciliation across all monorepo planes."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60"]
      :tasks [
        "T416MetaResearch"
        "T416DesignSystem"
        "T416AlgoSearch"
        "T416Coordination"
        "T416SelfCorrect"
        "T416Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Enables autonomous agents to perform high-assurance research and iterative refinement")
        (:pos "Delivers 50-70% token savings on vector graphics and design specifications via native ASN")
        (:pos "Prevents algorithmic bottlenecks while avoiding premature overengineering")
        (:neg "Requires all research and design proposals to undergo formal two-pass validation before implementation")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D61"
      :shortcode "D61"
      :title "Agent Goal Perception, Semantic Validation Primitives, and Epistemic Infrastructure Readiness"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Attention-based language models lack intrinsic deliberation loops and often mistake linguistic fluency for goal comprehension. Without rigid mathematical and operational grounding, agents exhibit goal drift across multi-turn trajectories, premature victory claims, and superficial satisfaction of prompt requests without fulfilling underlying architectural invariants."
      :drivers [
        "Epistemic Operationalization: Define goal comprehension strictly as the ability to construct a falsifiable verification gate before mutating state"
        "Deliberation Gap Elimination: Overcome feed-forward attention limits via structured intent schemas"
        "Physical Receipt Verification: Forbid speculative self-grading by requiring immutable execution evidence with non-vacuous assertion counts"
        "Multi-Lens Triangulation: Validate all complex goals across theoretical bounds, runtime telemetry, and adversarial falsification"
        "Typestate Isolation: Prevent cognitive goal degradation by bounding operational scopes to cohesive 120-280 line state machines"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0061 (D61) establishing the normative standard for Agent Goal Perception and Validation across the AgentScript ecosystem. Codify the 4-level Goal Hierarchy, benchmark full monorepo infrastructure readiness, and deploy the discrete Semantic Goal Validator."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61"]
      :tasks [
        "T416MetaResearch"
        "T416DesignSystem"
        "T416AlgoSearch"
        "T416Coordination"
        "T416SelfCorrect"
        "T416Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates premature settlement and hallucinatory victory declarations monorepo-wide")
        (:pos "Grounds every goal in a machine-executable, falsifiable verification predicate")
        (:pos "Provides transparent infrastructure readiness criteria for all external agent IDE integrations")
        (:neg "Requires all work items to declare explicit falsifiable gates and non-vacuous assertions")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D62"
      :shortcode "D62"
      :title "Dynamic Paradigm Specialization, Universal Third-Party Harness, and Composable Chaining Pipelines"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Universal harnesses targeting third-party agent systems must accommodate diverse model capacities ranging from Frontier models to edge SLMs. While Frontier models can digest all specializations simultaneously, monolithic prompt injection incurs heavy TTFT, operational cost penalties, and attention dispersal. Interactive REPL sessions require open-ended broad specializations, whereas headless CLI invocations offer a single deterministic leverage point (the orchestrator chokepoint) to curate context, enforce modular paradigm projection, and manage pipeline chaining without context spillover."
      :drivers [
        "Headless Orchestrator Chokepoint: Leverage the headless CLI entrypoint as the single physical governance gateway for context filtering and paradigm projection"
        "Frontier vs SLM Tiered Allocation: Support omni-specialization for Frontier models while providing strictly bounded single-paradigm projections for edge SLMs"
        "REPL vs Headless Functional Partition: Maintain broad ambient exploration in interactive REPL while enforcing task-directed minimal envelopes in headless runs"
        "Composable Paradigm Chaining: Enable sequential pipeline transitions with epistemic clean airgaps to eliminate cognitive bleedover"
        "Semantic Subword & CamelCase Alignment: Enforce morpheme-aligned CamelCase identifiers and bare alphanumeric markers across all harness schemas"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0062 (D62) establishing Dynamic Paradigm Specialization (DPS) and the Universal Third-Party Harness Architecture. Partition harness execution into Broad Interactive REPL and Laser Headless Chokepoint modes. Formalize modular paradigm manifests in harness/paradigms/. Implement dynamic specialization projection in harness context assembly with epistemic airgap truncation between chained pipeline wagons."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62"]
      :tasks [
        "T417HarnessChokepoint"
        "T417DynamicParadigmRegistry"
        "T417FrontierOmniAdapter"
        "T417ComposableChainAirgap"
        "T417ReplHeadlessPartition"
        "T417Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Enables third-party tools and CLI agents to execute high-assurance tasks at minimal token cost")
        (:pos "Eliminates attention dispersal and instruction drift in multi-paradigm workflows")
        (:pos "Prevents cognitive bias from leaking across chained agent transitions")
        (:neg "Requires headless callers to declare task intent or accept default dynamic heuristic projection")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D63"
      :shortcode "D63"
      :title "Visual Monitoring Substrate, 4-Tier Audit Framework, Cross-Platform Integration, and Jira-Based Multidimensional Analysis"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "While the core AgentScript ecosystem excels in sub-5ms AST intelligence, deterministic VFS operations, and pure ASN machine memory, it lacks an integrated visual observability plane. Monitoring agent sessions, task backlogs, active wave DAGs, and physical execution receipts relies on text dumps or fragmented TUI fragments locked within individual packages. Furthermore, cross-platform enterprise engineering requires seamless synchronization with Jira Cloud/Data Center, structured 4-tier audit cadences (sub-second in-memory checks up to global multi-mesh audits), and unified visual projections across terminal, web, and desktop environments without introducing heavy third-party dependencies."
      :drivers [
        "Unified Triple-Projection Model: Single canonical in-memory ASN telemetry state projected simultaneously into Terminal TUI, Web Dashboard, and Desktop/Browser Sidepanel"
        "4-Tier Graduated Audit Framework: Stratifying verification into Tier 1 Quick In-Memory, Tier 2 Commit-Based, Tier 3 Task/Wave Milestone, and Tier 4 Global Holistic Multi-Mesh"
        "Bidirectional Jira Multidimensional Integration: Synchronizing Jira issues with machine-native task ledgers, mapping sprint velocity against epistemic veracity, token density, and architectural boundaries"
        "Canonical Package Restructuring: Extracting packages/asl-view and packages/asl-jira to eliminate UI duplication across agent, harness, and browser-plugin"
        "Cross-Platform High-Assurance Runtime: Ensuring deterministic execution across macOS, Linux, and Windows with zero foreign dependencies"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0063 (D63) establishing the Visual Monitoring Substrate, 4-Tier Audit Framework, and Jira-Based Multidimensional Analysis Standard. Author Phase 418 / Wave 70 to formalize the 4-tier audit cadences, specify the unified triple-projection architecture in packages/asl-view, codify the bidirectional Jira synchronization bridge, and execute cross-platform research and package restructuring plans."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63"]
      :tasks [
        "T418AuditTiers"
        "T418VisualDashboard"
        "T418JiraIntegration"
        "T418CrossPlatformResearch"
        "T418SystemRestructuring"
        "T418Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Provides real-time visibility into agent reasoning, wave DAG progress, KV-cache telemetry, and task receipts")
        (:pos "Bridges enterprise Jira project management with immutable cryptographic execution receipts")
        (:pos "Eliminates UI and rendering fragmentation across monorepo packages through unified asl-view substrate")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining bidirectional Jira issue state mapping alongside git-native task ledgers")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D64"
      :shortcode "D64"
      :title "Human Resonance, Reflexive Cognitive Psychology, Sociological Diffusion, Market Utility, and Real-World Business Modeling Paradigms"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Traditional autonomous agent paradigms operate almost exclusively in inward-facing computational domains: syntax checking, AST refactoring, and deterministic gate evaluation. However, software and autonomous agents are fundamentally socio-technical systems that succeed or fail based on their ability to perceive, resonate with, and solve problems for real human audiences, businesses, and markets. Without formal paradigms for audience resonance, reflexive psychological analysis, jobs-to-be-done utility validation, sociological diffusion, and sustainable unit economics, agents produce technically correct artifacts that suffer from user rejection, cognitive dissonance, misaligned incentives, or commercial invalidity."
      :drivers [
        "Reflexive Theory of Mind (ToM) & Recursive Perception: Formalizing Vladimir Lefebvre reflexive control and multi-level cognitive modeling where agents model how human users model the system"
        "Audience Resonance & Aesthetic Mechanics: Calibrating semantic gravity, narrative alignment, and perceptual signal-to-noise ratio to ensure communications attract and retain human attention"
        "Jobs-To-Be-Done (JTBD) & Problem-Solution Fit: Decomposing human needs into functional, emotional, and social jobs, establishing strict threshold checks for pain severity"
        "Behavioral Economics & Choice Architecture: Integrating Kahneman System 1 intuitive heuristics and System 2 deliberative pacing, minimizing cognitive fatigue"
        "Sociological Network Diffusion & Memetics: Modeling memetic transmission, tribal alignment, social proof dynamics, and multi-stakeholder game theory"
        "Modern Agentic Business Modeling & App Formats: Codifying value creation, delivery, and capture architectures across next-generation formats"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0064 (D64) establishing the comprehensive Human Resonance, Reflexive Cognitive Psychology, Sociological Diffusion, Market Utility, and Real-World Business Modeling Paradigms. Author Phase 419 / Wave 71 to formalize specialized paradigm specifications in harness/paradigms/, establish executable cognitive and reflexive evaluation suites, integrate audience resonance heuristics into agent feedback loops, and codify modern agentic business model formats."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64"]
      :tasks [
        "T419ReflexiveTheoryOfMind"
        "T419AudienceResonanceAndAesthetics"
        "T419ProblemUtilityAndJTBD"
        "T419BehavioralPsychologyAndChoice"
        "T419SociologicalDiffusionAndNetworks"
        "T419AgenticBusinessModelsAndAppFormats"
        "T419Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Equips autonomous agents with rigorous socio-cognitive models for human interaction, eliminating cold mechanical rejection")
        (:pos "Bridges computer science engineering with real-world market validation, behavioral economics, and sustainable monetization")
        (:pos "Provides formal homoiconic ASN schemas for business model canvases, customer journey maps, and reflexive state trees")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining psychological and market domain ontology alongside low-level AST and VFS primitives")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D65"
      :shortcode "D65"
      :title "Multi-Project Orchestration, Resident Daemon Launch Strategy, and Distributed Peer Mesh Network Architecture"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Managing autonomous coding agents across multi-project environments currently suffers from daemon fragmentation and socket quarantine failures. On-demand lazy spawning from within sandboxed shells inherits restricted capabilities, causing socket permission errors and blocking netcat stalls. Furthermore, orchestrating linked repositories with a central AntiGravity manager requires non-interfering VFS partitioning, cross-project buffer mutexes, and an autonomous peer mesh network that seamlessly bridges local Unix Domain Sockets with remote build and inference nodes across machines."
      :drivers [
        "Persistent Supervisor Lifecycle: Replacing fragile on-demand shell spawning with an OS-level user service (launchd on macOS, systemd on Linux) binding ~/.asl/run/hub.sock outside IDE sandbox restrictions"
        "Central AntiGravity Session Hub: Implementing multi-project session routing where a single resident hub manages independent VFS memory partitions keyed by workspace root hashes"
        "Cross-Project Buffer Mutex & Lease Engine: Utilizing agent-bus MutexRegistry to prevent concurrent multi-agent write collisions across linked monorepos and micro-apps"
        "Autonomous Cross-Machine Peer Mesh: Federating local UDS connections with remote TLS/WebSocket nodes via self-framing ASN transport streams, distributed heartbeats, and dropout task stealing"
        "Non-Blocking IPC Dispatcher: Replacing blocking 2-second netcat shell checks with non-blocking socket probing to permanently eliminate CLI execution freezes"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0065 (D65) establishing the Multi-Project Orchestration, Resident Daemon Launch Strategy, and Distributed Peer Mesh Network Architecture Standard. Author Phase 420 / Wave 72 to formalize the central hub routing model, implement cross-project buffer lease protection, configure launchd/systemd service descriptors, refactor socket client probing to non-blocking mode, and verify distributed mesh coordination."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65"]
      :tasks [
        "T420DaemonLaunchSupervisor"
        "T420CentralHubRouting"
        "T420CrossProjectMutexRegistry"
        "T420DistributedMeshTopology"
        "T420NonBlockingSocketClient"
        "T420Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Enables seamless multi-project orchestration under a single authoritative AntiGravity manager")
        (:pos "Eliminates process stalls, socket permission denials, and 2-second netcat latency penalties")
        (:pos "Provides cross-machine capability discovery and distributed task resilience against peer dropouts")
        (:neg "Requires initial one-time user service registration for system-level supervisor activation")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D66"
      :shortcode "D66"
      :title "Runtime Substrate De-Bloat, Netcat Eradication, and Ghost Architecture Pruning"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "The runtime substrate accumulated vestigial dependencies across historical system epochs: fragile netcat (nc -U) shell piping, dead Node.js fallbacks, powershell branches, and simulated Watch Dog components inherited from early Jaios and Eddie OS models. These components introduce 2-second CLI stalls, cross-platform breakage (BSD vs GNU netcat), sandbox permission denials, and artificial APM telemetry bloat without providing real-world runtime protection."
      :drivers [
        "Elimination of Netcat IPC: Netcat is non-portable, sandbox-restricted, and introduces 2-second stalls; replace with direct in-process dispatch or Python native non-blocking socket probing"
        "Ghost Architecture Pruning: Decouple Watch Dog from telemetry metrics and eliminate simulated APM alert structures in favor of simple STDIN=/dev/null redirection and process timeouts"
        "Legacy Runtime Liquidation: Purge dead NODE_BIN, EVAL_RUNNER, and Windows powershell code paths from asl/asl to restore zero-foreign purity"
        "Deterministic In-Process Execution: Prioritize direct sub-80ms in-memory execution via asl-engine over fragile persistent daemon socket plumbing"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0066 (D66) establishing the Runtime Substrate De-Bloat, Netcat Eradication, and Ghost Architecture Pruning Standard. Author Phase 421 / Wave 73 to eliminate nc -U from the CLI dispatcher, purge legacy Node.js fallbacks, decouple Watch Dog from telemetry, and enforce direct deterministic in-process execution."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66"]
      :tasks [
        "T421NetcatEradication"
        "T421WatchdogGhostPruning"
        "T421LegacyNodeAndPowershellPurge"
        "T421Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Completely eliminates 2-second netcat delays and sandbox socket permission failures")
        (:pos "Prunes ghost APM metrics and simplifies process supervision across the codebase")
        (:pos "Eliminates legacy Node.js and shell crutches, restoring true zero-foreign alignment")
        (:neg "Requires refactoring legacy netcat call sites in asl/asl")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D67"
      :shortcode "D67"
      :title "Conceptual Milestones, Retrospective Practice, and Pragmatic Observability"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Granular task ledgers (.asl/mem/tasks/) and raw execution receipts (receipts.asn) drown high-level system comprehension in micro-step clutter. Teams lack a macro-level conceptual changelog that records why architectural epochs occurred, what research discoveries were made, what design decisions were taken, and what retrospective lessons were learned. Furthermore, observability lacks pragmatic multidimensional grounding across macro milestones and execution tiers."
      :drivers [
        "Macro-Level Conceptual Changelog: Tracking system evolution at the milestone level (Epoch/Milestone) rather than individual tasks or toolcalls"
        "Structured Retrospective Practice: Systematic adversarial scrutiny at wave/milestone boundaries to evaluate what worked, identify friction, and prune dead abstractions"
        "Progressive Hindsight Refinement: Updating retrospective entries over time as discoveries mature"
        "4-Tier Pragmatic Observability: Structuring monitoring from Tier 1 (micro syntax checks) to Tier 4 (5D epistemic consistency) without synthetic APM bloat"
        "Machine-Native Homoiconic Storage: Storing retrospectives in pure ASN (.asl/mem/retrospectives.asn) queryable via CLI and projectable on-demand"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0067 (D67) establishing the Conceptual Milestones, Retrospective Practice, and Pragmatic Observability Standard. Author Phase 422 / Wave 74 to codify the canonical retrospective schema, initialize .asl/mem/retrospectives.asn, implement CLI query tooling, and bind 4-tier observability into the sovereign consistency engine."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67"]
      :tasks [
        "T422MilestoneLedgerCodification"
        "T422RetrospectiveProtocolEngine"
        "T422ObservabilityTiersIntegration"
        "T422Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Provides crystal-clear macro visibility into the evolution, intent, and research findings of the system")
        (:pos "Establishes a continuous self-healing discipline to prune architectural debt before it hardens")
        (:pos "Bridges high-level governance with executable, physical 4-tier verification receipts")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining milestone entries at major architectural boundaries")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D68"
      :shortcode "D68"
      :title "Hierarchical Memory Scoping, Package Independence, and Transient Workspace Topology"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Monolithic memory architectures concentrate all tasks, backlogs, and retrospectives into a single root directory (.asl/mem/), causing severe cognitive sprawl, git merge collisions across concurrent agent work, and context pollution for local package maintenance. Sub-packages lack localized domain memory, while the root workspace conflates long-term architectural truth with transient search caches and exploratory hypotheses."
      :drivers [
        "Package-Scoped Local Memory (<pkg>/mem/): Local backlogs, micro-tasks, and retrospectives isolated to their domain, eliminating root noise and git merge collisions"
        "Repository-Scoped Sovereign Memory (<repo>/.asl/mem/): Authoritative source of truth for cross-package ADRs, system intent, master roadmaps, and physical verification receipts"
        "Root Workspace Transient Isolation (<root>/.asl/): Confining disposable BM25 inverted indices, scratch hypotheses, and active in-flight session buffers to ephemeral storage"
        "Cross-Repository ASL Mesh Coordination (agent-bus): Seamless peer federation across neighboring repositories via ASN wire protocol, workspace hash partitioning, and buffer mutex leases"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0068 (D68) establishing the Hierarchical Memory Scoping, Package Independence, and Transient Workspace Topology Standard. Authorize sub-packages to maintain localized mem/ directories (backlog, tasks, retrospectives), reserve root .asl/mem/ for repository-wide governance, dedicate root .asl/ to transient runtime caches, and coordinate multi-repo orchestration through agent-bus."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67" "D68"]
      :tasks [
        "T422MilestoneLedgerCodification"
        "T422RetrospectiveProtocolEngine"
        "T422ObservabilityTiersIntegration"
        "T422Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates root task pollution and enables independent package development without merge contention")
        (:pos "Strictly separates long-term architectural truth from disposable in-memory caches and scratch hypotheses")
        (:pos "Enables seamless multi-project orchestration under a single AntiGravity manager via agent-bus")
        (:neg "Requires consistency audit to traverse both repository and package-level memory directories")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D69"
      :shortcode "D69"
      :title "Paradigm Institutionalization of Audit Discoveries, Static Binary Anomaly Detection, and Strict Whitelisting"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "When technical audits uncover architectural incongruities or foreign binary crutches (such as netcat, hidden Node.js fallbacks, or ghost watchdogs), treating them as isolated bugfixes allows identical defects to recur in downstream modules. Furthermore, without static verification of binary provenance, unregistered third-party tools silently contaminate developer workflows, scripts, and production environments."
      :drivers [
        "Paradigm Institutionalization: Every uncovered audit anomaly must be codified into the system paradigm (harness/paradigm.asn) and audit rubric (harness/audit-protocols.asn) as an immutable negative rule"
        "Static Binary Anomaly Detection: Automated static analysis scanning shell launchers and execution dispatchers to detect unregistered CLI binary invocations before runtime"
        "Strict Binary Whitelist (.asl.config.asn): Explicit declaration of all permitted host binaries (python3, git, bash); all undeclared binaries are rejected statically"
        "Zero-Foreign Provenance: Complete boundary protection ensuring downstream projects and packages cannot introduce hidden toolchain dependencies"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0069 (D69) establishing the Paradigm Institutionalization of Audit Discoveries, Static Binary Anomaly Detection, and Strict Whitelisting Standard. Codify audit-institutionalization and strict-binary-whitelist axioms in harness/paradigm.asn, add the unregistered-binary-anomaly category to harness/audit-protocols.asn, define the canonical binary-whitelist in .asl.config.asn, and enforce static whitelist verification under monorepo gates."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67" "D68" "D69"]
      :tasks [
        "T423ParadigmCodification"
        "T423AuditTaxonomyExtension"
        "T423BinaryWhitelistConfig"
        "T423StaticWhitelistLinter"
        "T423Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Mathematically prevents regression of past audit issues by turning findings into permanent paradigm axioms")
        (:pos "Statically eliminates rogue third-party binaries from appearing in downstream projects or shell scripts")
        (:pos "Provides 100 percent dependency provenance across all toolplane layers")
        (:neg "Requires explicit registration in .asl.config.asn for any new external host tool")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D70"
      :shortcode "D70"
      :title "Universal Dependency Justification, Interconnected Cluster Mapping, and Periodic Audit Protocol"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Dependencies across software ecosystems silently proliferate without documented architectural rationale. In AI-native agent workspaces, third-party libraries and host binaries introduce supply-chain vulnerabilities, cognitive bloat, hidden coupling, and performance degradation. When dependencies are treated as isolated line items rather than interconnected clusters (such as web UI React, Vite, and Tailwind stacks), removing or modifying one component causes cascading failures. Furthermore, absent scheduled reassessment cycles, ephemeral or suboptimal dependencies harden into permanent technical debt."
      :drivers [
        "Universal Dependency-Justification Principle: Every dependency (binary, package, library) must possess an explicit machine-readable rationale, risk rating, and replacement vector in .asl/mem/dependencies.asn"
        "Interconnected Cluster Topology: Dependencies operating as tightly-coupled subgraphs must be modeled as cohesive clusters, preventing partial removal regressions and establishing atomic compensating migration sagas"
        "Proactive Pruning of Minor and Ephemeral Dependencies: Flagging minor dependencies (such as lucide-react or unvetted wrappers) for replacement by native AgentScript primitives (asl-svg, pure VDOM)"
        "Periodic Technology Reassessment Protocol: Mandatory quarterly reassessments enforced via 'asl audit dependencies' to review optimality, license drift, and functional overhead"
        "Concrete Action Extraction: Converting high-level research recommendations into discrete, prioritized tasks rather than speculative documentation"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0070 (D70) establishing the Universal Dependency Justification, Interconnected Cluster Mapping, and Periodic Audit Protocol. Codify the central dependency registry in .asl/mem/dependencies.asn, map coupled clusters, implement 'asl audit dependencies' in the core toolchain, schedule replacement milestones for high-overhead packages, and enforce dependency justification across all monorepo verification gates."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67" "D68" "D69" "D70"]
      :tasks [
        "T424DependencyInventoryAndRegistry"
        "T424WebClusterInterconnectMapping"
        "T424ToolchainBinaryPruning"
        "T424PeriodicAuditProtocolEngine"
        "T424Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Guarantees 100 percent justification and traceability for all binaries and libraries in the workspace")
        (:pos "Eliminates cascading build breaks by managing interconnected clusters as unified atomic topologies")
        (:pos "Provides automated static verification via 'asl audit dependencies' to reject unjustified or stale dependencies")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining explicit dependency records and scheduled quarterly reassessment dates in .asl/mem/dependencies.asn")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D71"
      :shortcode "D71"
      :title "Composable Observability Architecture, Per-Project Tool Metrics, and ESL Worktree Lifecycle Telemetry"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :problem "Monolithic logging and uncoordinated metrics in multi-agent toolchains pollute repository histories, induce context bloat, and blur component boundaries. Web search APIs, ephemeral git worktrees, and toolplane dispatch lack localized metric accounting, while excessive log retention wastes developer and model attention. Without an isolated yet composable observability layer, agents cannot tune tool performance, track rate limits, or trace worktree lifecycles back to sovereign branches."
      :drivers [
        "Per-Project WebSearch Telemetry: Track query volume, engine quotas, provider latency, and rate-limit limitations in git-ignored stores (.asl/metrics/webSearch.asn)"
        "ESL Worktree Lifecycle Integration: Track worktree creation, automated cleanup tombstones, and source-branch annotated metric sync to main (.asl/metrics/worktrees.asn)"
        "Toolplane Usage & Limitation Tuning: Capture p50 and p95 execution latencies, error frequencies, and boundary ceiling hits to guide runtime tuning"
        "Adaptive Log Retention Ratios: Enforce 1:10 routine downsampling vs 1:1 lossless failure retention with 256KB compaction caps and 14 to 30 day TTLs"
        "Composable Isolated Observability: Maintain strict component boundaries where each tool or subsystem manages its own telemetry, composable on demand via asl metrics"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0071 (D71) establishing the Composable Observability Architecture, Per-Project Tool Metrics, and ESL Worktree Lifecycle Telemetry Standard. Codify isolated metric stores in .asl/metrics/, ignore them from git, integrate worktree lifecycle tracking with source-branch sync, implement adaptive retention ratios, and provide the on-demand asl metrics aggregation engine."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67" "D68" "D69" "D70" "D71"]
      :tasks [
        "T425WebSearchPerProjectMetrics"
        "T425WorktreeLifecycleESL"
        "T425ToolLimitationTelemetry"
        "T425ComposableObservabilityAggregator"
        "T425Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Provides crystal-clear per-project visibility into WebSearch quotas, provider health, and query latencies")
        (:pos "Eliminates git history pollution by isolating metrics to git-ignored compact ASN stores")
        (:pos "Enables safe, conflict-free multi-worktree execution with source-branch attribution")
        (:pos "Reduces log volume by over 85 percent via 1:10 downsampling and compact S-expression serialization")
        (:neg "Requires tool dispatchers to emit metric events on invocation")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D72"
      :shortcode "D72"
      :title "Browser-Based Demonstration System, Configurable Harnesses, and Specialized Presets"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/browser-demonstration"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Demonstrating and deploying small language models (<3B) in client browser sandboxes requires strict boundary enforcement, dynamic harness specialization, and deterministic preset grounding. Generic monolithic prompts overwhelm sub-billion models with negative attractor tokens and unbounded contexts, inducing catastrophic amnesia or grammar collapse. Unstructured playgrounds fail to expose hard mathematical failure horizons, while client runtimes must seamlessly switch between single-threaded WASM and multi-threaded WebWorker/OffscreenCanvas pipelines without UI stutter or tab eviction."
      :drivers [
        "Browser Ceiling & Model Tier Calibration: Enforce strict 3B parameter ceiling, evaluate SmolLM2 (135M, 360M, 1.7B) alongside Qwen2.5 (0.5B, 1.5B, 3B), and calibrate threshold parameters (TTFT < 50ms, RAM < 2.2GB, schema overhead < 150 tokens)"
        "Specialized Affirmative Harnesses: Implement capability-targeted harnesses for SVG vector graphics, reactive VDOM website generation, interactive toy/physics simulations, and spatial DOM perception with streaming FSM delimiter masks"
        "Demonstration Presets Library: Codify 12 executable presets in harness/results/browser_demonstration_presets.asn covering Conway Game of Life, Particle Spring Physics, Developer Portfolio, SaaS Pricing Matrix, Flowcharts, and Badges"
        "Single-Thread vs Multi-Thread Execution Contexts: Provide unified browser execution substrate supporting synchronous main-thread execution and dedicated WebWorker thread execution with SharedArrayBuffer and OffscreenCanvas"
        "Local Capability & Impossibility Studio: Build an interactive local gallery playground displaying achievable live demonstrations alongside mathematical impossibility boundaries"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0072 (D72) establishing the Browser-Based Demonstration System, Configurable Harnesses, and Specialized Presets Standard. Codify the 4-tier model calibration matrix under the 3B ceiling, integrate SmolLM2-135M as the primary delimiter guard, provide specialized affirmative harnesses for SVGs, websites, and toys, establish single-thread and multi-thread execution abstractions, and deliver the local interactive demonstration gallery."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61" "D62" "D63" "D64" "D65" "D66" "D67" "D68" "D69" "D70" "D71" "D72"]
      :tasks [
        "T426SmolLmResearchAndCalibration"
        "T426ConfigurableHarnessEngine"
        "T426DemonstrationPresetsCatalog"
        "T426LocalGalleryPlayground"
        "T426Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Guarantees zero-crash browser sandbox execution by strictly enforcing the 3B parameter ceiling")
        (:pos "Achieves 96+ percent schema fidelity on sub-billion models via affirmative prompts and streaming FSM masks")
        (:pos "Delivers 60fps responsive UI during heavy generation via multi-thread WebWorker and SharedArrayBuffer offloading")
        (:pos "Provides concrete grounded demonstration presets across toys, websites, and vector SVGs")
        (:neg "Requires WebGPU and WebWorker support for multi-thread 3B execution")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D73"
      :shortcode "D73"
      :title "Voice-In Action-Out Pipeline, Parakeet-TDT ASR Ingestion, Hanes Model Gallery, and Task Rendering Presets"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "architecture/voice-and-browser-gallery"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "Voice interaction in browser agent environments requires instant interruptibility, low-latency audio capture without audio synthesis overhead, 1-pass intent routing between chat search and autonomous action execution, and zero-friction 1-click model provisioning. Traditional setups overburden users with manual configuration knobs, unoptimized multi-tool prompts, and heavy TTS overhead, while failing to expose empirical hardware calibration metrics (VRAM, TTFT, TPS)."
      :drivers [
        "Dual-Mode Audio Capture & Instant Abort: Support click-to-toggle and hold-to-talk state machines (250ms threshold) wired directly to active AbortController tokens interrupting running agent tasks"
        "Raw ASR Ingestion & Zero-TTS Architecture: Stream raw uncorrected Parakeet-TDT-v3 transcripts directly into Hanes SLMs without text-to-speech overhead or pre-processing pipeline bloat"
        "1-Pass Intent Routing & Task Rendering Presets: Route transcripts to either Informational Chat with Live Google Search or Direct Agent CDP Action, rendering into specialized UI presets (:fast-search, :agent-action, :deep-synthesis, :codePatch)"
        "Zero-Friction Model Gallery & Calibration Stand: Provide 1-click model downloading via in-browser Cache API, automated hardware benchmark stand (VRAM, TTFT, TPS), and flagship Qwen 2.5 3B showcase with sane default parameters"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0073 (D73) establishing the Voice-In Action-Out Pipeline, Parakeet-TDT ASR Ingestion, Hanes Model Gallery, and Task Rendering Presets Standard. Enforce zero-configuration sane defaults with a 3-tier model selector (Nano 100M, Small 1.1GB, Smart 2.2GB), codify the dual-mode audio state machine with abort controller, implement 1-pass intent routing, and deliver the automated hardware calibration stand."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D71" "D72" "D73"]
      :tasks [
        "T427AudioCaptureStateMachineAndAbortController"
        "T427HanesVoiceGatewayAndParakeetIntegration"
        "T427TaskRenderingPresetsAndIntentRouter"
        "T427ModelGalleryCalibrationAndShowcase"
        "T427Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Enables instantaneous sub-second voice-to-action dispatch without text-to-speech latency or VRAM footprint")
        (:pos "Provides immediate task cancellation when recording terminates via synchronous AbortController propagation")
        (:pos "Eliminates configuration fatigue by applying pre-calibrated sane defaults to the 3-tier model selector")
        (:pos "Delivers 1-pass intent routing to specialized UI rendering presets across search and agent actions")
        (:neg "Requires WebGPU and local audio capture microphone permissions in client browser")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D74"
      :shortcode "D74"
      :title "Full Ecosystem Integrity, Redundancy Pruning, Token Efficiency and Untapped Potential Master Audit"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-10"
      :cluster "governance/master-audit"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "The rapid evolution of the AgentScript sovereign ecosystem across 35 packages, 825 source modules, 182 test suites, and 79 execution waves has accumulated latent architectural divergence, uncoordinated cross-package duplication, legacy kebab-case naming debt (1614 tokens), and unexploited subsystems (e-graphs, WASI compilation, ambient voice REPL, crawler). An exhaustive, ordered, and falsifiable master audit plan is required to systematically inspect every package and feature, audit integrity against foundational invariants (C1-C5, D1-D73), identify redundant code and dead weight for liquidation, verify token economy (SNR >= 0.75), and synthesize an authoritative architectural roadmap of untapped capabilities for the Grand Auditor."
      :drivers [
        "Holistic 100% Codebase Coverage: Every single repository, package, and feature suite must be scheduled into an explicit, ordered task with a deterministic verification gate"
        "Three-Pillar Evaluation Criteria: Every inspection must rigorously measure (1) Integrity against formal invariants, (2) Redundancy and dead code for liquidation, and (3) Token efficiency and CamelCase optimization (D51)"
        "Exploration of Untapped Potential: Subsystems with unrealized potential (E-Graphs in compiler passes, WASI AoT standalone runtime, Parakeet Voice in CLI/IDE, Autonomous Crawler in dialectical RAG) must be audited for immediate practical activation"
        "Sequential Execution & Grand Auditor Synthesis: The audit must be structured for sequential execution item-by-item, culminating in a final meta-analysis synthesizing invariants, candidates for removal, required additions, and strategic vectors"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0074 (D74) codifying the Master Audit Plan (Phase 428, Wave 80) across all 35 packages and subsystems. Establish 18 atomic work items adhering to the Enriched Task Context Standard (D52), enforce the 4-stage epistemic loop (Awareness, Planning, Reflection, Reconciliation), and mandate the Grand Auditor Synthesis Protocol as the final terminal deliverable."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D70" "D71" "D72" "D73" "D74"]
      :tasks [
        "T428AuditAslCoreLanguageAndParser"
        "T428AuditAslTypeCheckerAndCodegenWasm"
        "T428AuditAslShProcessEngineAndGitIntegration"
        "T428AuditAslCodecTextAndSvgTranspilation"
        "T428AuditAslGatesLintingAndRpcDispatcher"
        "T428AuditHarnessRuntimeSlmCalibrationAndLlmProtocol"
        "T428AuditAgentSwarmFsmAndCoreMiddleware"
        "T428AuditAgentBusMeshAndDistributedIpc"
        "T428AuditMemEngineVfsEgraphsAndAmnesia"
        "T428AuditIntelAstGraphAndHotspotCoverage"
        "T428AuditWebSearchAndDialecticalRag"
        "T428AuditVdomAndDualPerceptionUiEngine"
        "T428AuditVoicePipelineVadAndAddieRepl"
        "T428AuditPeripheralSubsystems"
        "T428AuditThirdPartySkillsEcosystemAndProjections"
        "T428AuditGovernanceDecisionsIntentAndTokenConventions"
        "T428GrandAuditorSynthesisAndOptimizationBlueprint"
        "T428Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Provides an exhaustive, reproducible, and verifiable roadmap for the Grand Auditor")
        (:pos "Identifies dead code, obsolete scripts, and redundant helpers across all 35 packages for safe liquidation")
        (:pos "Uncovers and operationalizes high-value latent capabilities such as compiler E-graphs and standalone WASI")
        (:pos "Saves an estimated 1600+ BPE tokens via systematic CamelCase and modular alias convergence")
        (:neg "Requires dedicated sequential auditing passes across the entire 825-module monorepo")
      ])
    (:decision
      :id "D75"
      :shortcode "D75"
      :title "Universal WebAssembly Ambient Substrate, Self-Contained Micro-Binary Packaging, and Regulated Platform Leaves Standard"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-11"
      :cluster "architecture/runtime"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "AgentScript previously utilized Rust as an intermediate compilation step to generate native binaries, imposing a 1.5 GB Cargo/LLVM toolchain burden, slow compilation cycles, and an impedance mismatch with S-expression AST semantics."
      :drivers [
        "WebAssembly as Ambient Substrate: The entire AgentScript core runtime, agent harness, memory ledger, and compiler must execute natively within WebAssembly (WASM/WASI)"
        "Zero-Rust Developer Distribution: The native CLI binary (asl) must be packaged as a self-contained micro-executable (<1.5 MB) via lightweight C micro-runtimes or OS-native JavaScriptCore"
        "Regulated Platform Leaves: Rust, Go, Embedded C, SwiftUI, Jetpack Compose, and JSX are preserved and strictly regulated as peripheral, export-only targets"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0075 (D75) establishing WebAssembly as the universal ambient substrate and primary compilation target for AgentScript, packaging a minimal self-contained native binary (<1.5 MB) with zero Rust or Python dependencies, and regulating peripheral platform leaves."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D69" "D75"]
      :tasks [
        "T430WasmCoreSubstrate"
        "T430GoPlatformLeaf"
        "T430CompilerMultiTarget"
        "T430Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates the 1.5 GB Rust and LLVM toolchain burden from daily development and CI pipelines")
        (:pos "Enables true cross-platform portability across browsers, CLI, servers, and edge environments with a single WASM module")
        (:pos "Produces an ultra-compact (<1.5 MB) standalone native CLI binary with sub-2ms cold starts and <15 MB RSS")
      ])
    (:decision
      :id "D76"
      :shortcode "D76"
      :title "Universal MVCC, Software Transactional Memory, and Homoiconic Semantic 3-Way Merge Engine"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-11"
      :cluster "architecture/concurrency"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "In multi-agent collaborative execution, traditional file locks and git worktrees create contention, latency, and merge conflicts."
      :drivers [
        "Homoiconicity as Concurrency Substrate: Code, data, message frames, and execution DAGs are all first-class S-expressions"
        "Lock-Free Multi-Agent Parallelism: Agents must branch state freely in resident memory without disk writes or mutex stalls"
        "Software Transactional Memory: Multi-file changes spanning interfaces, implementations, and tests must commit atomically"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0076 (D76) establishing a Universal MVCC, Software Transactional Memory (STM), and Homoiconic S-Expression 3-Way Merge Engine across the AgentScript ecosystem."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D76"]
      :tasks [
        "T431UniversalHomoiconicAstMergeEngine"
        "T431MultiFileSoftwareTransactionalMemory"
        "T431MvccBranchingAgentBus"
        "T431ConcurrentTaskDagSplicing"
        "T431PromptRadixTreeAndSpeculativeFuzzing"
        "T431Settle"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates file lock contention and allows unlimited parallel agent swarms to edit code safely in resident memory")
        (:pos "Enables atomic multi-file commits with automatic AST-level conflict reconciliation")
      ])
    (:decision
      :id "D77"
      :shortcode "D77"
      :title "Universal Python Eradication, Pure ASL Self-Hosting, and Sovereign Resident Runtime Engine"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-11"
      :cluster "architecture/runtime"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "The developer CLI and resident daemon still depend on Python (asl/bin/asl-engine 190 KB and inline python3 -c snippets in asl/asl), violating the pure self-hosted language teleology."
      :drivers [
        "Zero-Python Sovereignty: The entire development and execution toolchain must operate without requiring Python on host"
        "Pure ASL Self-Hosting: All consistency, token, and polarity checks must execute as pure AgentScript modules natively"
        "Sovereign Resident Runtime Engine: Re-engineer asl-engine as a compiled native binary consolidating resident daemon functionality and eliminating foreign Python"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0077 (D77) establishing the complete eradication of Python from the repository, migrating CLI helpers to pure ASL modules, and deploying native compiled asl-engine."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D74" "D75" "D76" "D77"]
