        "Task43204"
        "Task43205"
        "Task43206"
        "Task43207"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Completely eliminates Python as a system dependency across development, CI, and agent execution")
        (:pos "Reduces resident engine memory footprint from 65 MB to <12 MB RSS via native WASM runtime")
        (:pos "Accelerates consistency audits and CLI invocations from 850ms to <15ms cold start")
      ])
    (:decision
      :id "D78"
      :shortcode "D78"
      :title "Cross-Platform WebAssembly Core Substrate, Browser Autonomous Runtime, and Native Engine Micro-Evaluation"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-11"
      :cluster "architecture/runtime"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "asl-eval depends on Apple JavaScriptCore.framework, preventing Linux/Windows portability. Browser agents require sovereign WebAssembly packaging (asl-core.wasm <150 KB) with in-memory VFS and zero-socket Batch RPC (<16 MB RAM, <3 ms latency). C99 engine rewrite into pure ASL is prioritized last."
      :drivers [
        "Cross-Platform Portability: Eradicate Apple-proprietary JavaScriptCore framework dependency in asl-eval"
        "WebAssembly First Substrate: Package asl-core.wasm (<150 KB) as sovereign ambient core substrate"
        "In-Browser Autonomous Runtime: Zero-socket direct memory RPC bridge (asl_rpc_dispatch) and in-memory VFS within browser bounds"
        "Engine Evaluation Consolidation: Consolidate evaluation into asl-engine and liquidate asl-eval"
        "Prioritized Migration Schedule: Treat C99 engine source rewrite into pure ASL as strictly lowest priority"
      ]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0078 (D78) establishing the cross-platform WebAssembly core substrate, in-browser autonomous runtime, and consolidated native engine evaluation, deferring C99 engine rewrite to final phase."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D75" "D77" "D78"]
      :tasks [
        "Task43301"
        "Task43302"
        "Task43303"
        "Task43304"
        "Task43305"
        "Task43306"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Eliminates Apple JavaScriptCore dependency, delivering cross-platform evaluation on Linux, Windows, and macOS")
        (:pos "Enables pure in-browser autonomous agent execution via asl-core.wasm (<150 KB) with zero sockets")
        (:pos "Consolidates binary surface area into single sovereign asl-engine binary")
        (:neg "Defers C99-to-ASL engine rewrite to a future post-runtime phase as directed by user priority")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D79"
      :shortcode "D79"
      :title "Sovereign Single-Binary ASL Consolidation: Unifying Engine, Eval, Compiler, Evolver, and Memory into a Self-Contained Dependency-Free Executable"
      :status :active
      :date "2026-09-11"
      :cluster "architecture/runtime"
      :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
      :problem "The AgentScript toolchain currently suffers from fragmented separation across three components: asl-engine (resident daemon binary), asl-eval (evaluator binary), and asl/asl (a bloated 7389-line shell script containing an embedded 3319-line Python transliterator and ad-hoc string manipulations). Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078)."
      :drivers ["Single Sovereign Binary" "Eliminate Engine Separation" "Remove Bloated Script" "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078)." "Isolate External Dependencies"]
      :decision "Adopt ADR-0079 consolidating engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into single native binary, retiring separate binaries and pruning shell script."
      :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D79"]
      :tasks [
        "Task43401"
        "Task43402"
        "Task43403"
        "Task43404"
        "Task43405"
        "Task43406"
      ]
      :consequences [
        (:pos "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078).")
        (:pos "Replaces 7389-line shell script with clean native binary ~250 KB")
        (:pos "Unifies daemon, evaluator, and compiler into single executable")
        (:pos "Isolates database drivers and external adapters into separate pluggable boundaries")
        (:neg "Requires maintaining consolidated C99 unified launcher source until pure ASL self-hosting pass")
      ])
    (:adr
      :id "D80"
      :shortcode "D80"
