      :review ".asl/mem/reviews/D82DesignPlanReview.asn"
      :problem "The ASL web surface mixes narrow shells, purple/indigo gradients, cosmic decoration and pill-heavy controls without an explicit prose/data width policy."
      :drivers ["Calm technical identity" "Progressive disclosure" "Measured prose and data widths" "Responsive accessible interaction" "Single token source"]
      :decision "Adopt the Instrumented Editorial frame with a 72rem reading shell, opt-in 80rem data canvas, one restrained signal accent, workbench surfaces and progressive evidence disclosure."
